WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:07.597
In this video, we'll
draft an unmoderated study

2
00:00:07.597 --> 00:00:10.849
of our favorite toolbar against the original.

3
00:00:10.849 --> 00:00:14.319
It's a hypothetical tonight:
nobody has research

4
00:00:14.319 --> 00:00:17.210
tool accounts, so it stops at the draft.

5
00:00:18.308 --> 00:00:23.315
With accounts, the same prompts would
create the study in a tool like Outset,

6
00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:28.322
and recruit through a panel like
User Interviews, then stop at your approval.

7
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:35.107
The draft: a 17-minute study
for six people who make

8
00:00:35.107 --> 00:00:39.373
diagrams at least weekly,
each trying both toolbars.

9
00:00:39.373 --> 00:00:43.230
Nothing was launched,
and no one was recruited.

10
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:50.350
It starts with the decision the
study should inform, then the setup,

11
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:54.107
with the exact version of each build,
so everyone tests the same thing.

12
00:00:58.952 --> 00:01:03.462
Then a short screener, the participant
script, and two timed tasks.

13
00:01:06.452 --> 00:01:10.998
Next, we'll turn study results
into findings, with real quotes.
